CALLING THE BOSS

197
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,707
- We have a problem here.
- What?

198
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:04,502
THE BOSS IS ON THE WAY

199
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:06,254
HE FINDS THE TAP FIXED IN PLACE

200
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:07,922
Right, it's for both.

201
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:12,051
When we do the dishes,
we might use too much water

202
00:09:12,134 --> 00:09:14,262
if we do it under a running tap.

203
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:15,721
So for the water,

204
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:19,308
we'll collect water in this bowl
shaped like a soy sauce dipping dish

205
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,018
and use it for as long as we can.

206
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:23,771
HE ONLY BUILT A TAP FOR THE JACUZZI
TO CONSERVE WATER

207
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,147
DIFFICULTY: HARD

208
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,691
Boss didn't think this through.

209
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,820
Should I cook the rice?

210
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:31,946
I'm good at it.

211
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:33,072
Yes, please.

212
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:38,911
HE MAKES RICE OUT OF GUILT

213
00:09:42,206 --> 00:09:43,040
Done.

214
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:44,750
Is the water amount right?

215
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:46,294
- The water? Yeah.
- Okay.

216
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:49,880
THE BOSS'S RICE IS READY TO BE COOKED

217
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:51,799
JUN-HO JOINS THE KITCHEN

218
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:53,509
- What should I do?
- You can rinse these.

219
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:54,552
- Rinse them?
- Yeah.

220
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:55,636
I should…

221
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,514
- I should rinse them here.
- Right.

222
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,308
- I'll just put them all in.
- Yeah.

223
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,268
YEON-KOUNG WASHES
AND PUTS THEM IN THE BOWL

224
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:04,395
THEN JUN-HO RINSES THEM

225
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:06,147
I'll put them over here.

226
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:07,273
ORGANIZES THEM ON THE SIDE

227
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:08,733
SQUATTING

228
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:09,942
RINSING

229
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,611
STANDING UP

230
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:13,696
ORGANIZING

231
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:19,660
Geez.

232
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:23,497
SQUATTING WHILE DISHWASHING

233
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:25,041
<i>I'm so hot.</i>

234
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:28,377
SUNKEN EYES

235
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:29,462
Are you okay, Jun-ho?

236
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:31,589
I'm so hot, Yeon-koung.

237
