00:44:37,174 --> 00:44:39,718
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes. It was actually hot.

1058
00:44:40,344 --> 00:44:44,598
AFTER CHECKING ON THE GUESTS,
HE GOES TO WASH UP

1059
00:44:53,941 --> 00:44:55,609
THE BOSS IS STILL ASLEEP

1060
00:44:55,692 --> 00:44:58,695
If no one else wakes up,
should we go running by ourselves?

1061
00:44:58,779 --> 00:44:59,780
Okay.

1062
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:01,365
THEY HOPE TO GO RUNNING AT 8:00 A.M.

1063
00:45:02,199 --> 00:45:03,409
Let's play <i>omok.</i>

1064
00:45:04,201 --> 00:45:05,702
THEY WILL PLAY OMOK WHILE WAITING

1065
00:45:05,786 --> 00:45:07,955
GO STONES & BOARD

1066
00:45:08,580 --> 00:45:10,916
HE WALKS CAREFULLY NOT TO WAKE OTHERS UP

1067
00:45:21,677 --> 00:45:23,137
The air is cold.

1068
00:45:23,887 --> 00:45:25,889
SURPRISED

1069
00:45:25,973 --> 00:45:28,100
Gosh, the air is cold.

1070
00:45:30,477 --> 00:45:31,562
QUIET AGAIN

1071
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:35,065
He's sleep-talking.

1072
00:45:41,655 --> 00:45:42,865
Geez, it's cold.

1073
00:45:42,948 --> 00:45:43,991
Good morning.

1074
00:45:44,074 --> 00:45:45,451
Hey, aren't you cold?

1075
00:45:45,534 --> 00:45:46,702
We were warm.

1076
00:45:47,953 --> 00:45:50,706
THE ONLY ONE THAT FEELS COLD

1077
00:45:54,209 --> 00:45:56,879
HE TAKES A SOCK OUT

1078
00:46:04,428 --> 00:46:05,679
Gosh, it's cold.

1079
00:46:10,267 --> 00:46:12,895
7:30 A.M.

1080
00:46:14,104 --> 00:46:17,441
YEON-KOUNG WAKES UP

1081
00:46:19,109 --> 00:46:23,071
SHE MAKES HER BED RIGHT AWAY

1082
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:33,999
IT'S NOT EASY TO GET OUT OF THE ROOM

1083
00:46:36,001 --> 00:46:37,002
Damn it.

1084
00:46:39,213 --> 00:46:40,255
Geez, what a pain.

1085
00:46:49,264 --> 00:46:51,808
7:55 A.M.

1086
00:46:51,892 --> 00:46:53,060
It's 8:00 a.m.

1087
00:46:54,353 --> 00:46:56,939
IT'S TIME TO GO RUNNING, BUT IT'S QUIET

1088
00:46:57,022 --> 00:46:58,232
Don-hee, should we go?

1089
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:00,692
THE TWO PLAN TO GO RUN BY THEMSELVES

1090
00:47:08,325 --> 00:47:09,284
Did you sleep well?

1091
00:47:09,910 --> 00:47:11,119
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes.

1092
00:47:11,703 --> 00:47:13,205
- Going out? Let's go.
- Yes.

1093
00:47:13,288 --> 00:47:14,122
Yes!

1094
00:47:14,206 --> 00:47:16,875
RUNNING PARTICIPANTS

1095
00:47:17,709 --> 00:47:19,169
JUN-HO ALSO WAKES UP TO RUN

1096
00:47:19,795 --> 00:47:22,548
RUNNING PARTICIPANTS

1097
00:47:22,631 --> 00:47:24,132
Shouldn't we wake Kian up?

1098
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:26,510
HE PROMISED TO RUN WITH THEM
BUT IS STILL ASLEEP

1099
00:47:27,135 --> 00:47:28,303
Wake him up.

1100
00:47:28,387 --> 00:47:29,763
Wake him up?

1101
00:47:31,848 --> 00:47:35,018
Kian, we're ready to go running.

1102
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:36,228
Already?

1103
00:47:36,311 --> 00:47:37,229
We were waiting.

1104
00:47:37,980 --> 00:47:38,814
Gosh.

1105
00:47:39,398 --> 00:47:40,232
SNEEZING

1106
00:47:41,191 --> 00:47:42,693
Are you all right, Boss?

1107
00:47:42,776 --> 00:47:44,903
I'm so cold.

1108
00:47:44,987 --> 00:47:47,197
HE STILL FEELS LETHARGIC

1109
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:49,032
You promised, so you have to go.

1110
00:47:49,575 --> 00:47:50,450
PRINCIPLED YEON-KOUNG

1111
00:47:50,534 --> 00:47:51,368
Let's go.

1112
00:47:54,705 --> 00:47:57,457
AS YEON-KOUNG SAID, HE KEEPS HIS PROMISE

1113
00:47:58,333 --> 00:47:59,209
Let's go.

1114
00:48:00,711 --> 00:48:03,255
Hey, you acted like you wouldn't run,
but you woke up early.

1115
00:48:03,338 --> 00:48:06,258
Come on, I used to be an athlete.
This is nothing.

1116
00:48:06,341 --> 00:48:08,343
I should at least be this diligent.

1117
00:48:08,427 --> 00:48:09,511
That's good.

1118
00:48:09,595 --> 00:48:10,429
EATS A SNACK

1119
00:48:10,512 --> 00:48:11,597
We have to open the door.

1120
00:48:12,180 --> 00:48:13,056
Push it open.

1121
00:48:13,140 --> 00:48:15,767
OPENING THE DOOR ON TIPTOE

1122
00:48:18,061 --> 00:48:19,104
Wait, you can reach it?

1123
00:48:20,105 --> 00:48:20,939
Of course.

1124
00:48:21,023 --> 00:48:22,107
You can reach it like this?

1125
00:48:22,190 --> 00:48:24,276
IT'S EASIER WHEN PUSHING IT OPEN

1126
00:48:25,652 --> 00:48:27,195
The weather is nice.

1127
00:48:27,279 --> 00:48:28,697
So this place looks like this.

1128
00:48:29,448 --> 00:48:31,199
- Let's go.
- Sure, let's go.

1129
00:48:33,702 --> 00:48:35,037
Are we starting from here?

1130
00:48:36,079 --> 00:48:38,624
Apparently, we might see cows on the way.

1131
00:48:38,707 --> 00:48:41,460
- Really?
- Yeah, they let their cows graze here.

1132
00:48:41,543 --> 00:48:42,753
Really?

1133
00:48:42,836 --> 00:48:44,796
THEY MIGHT RUN INTO COWS

1134
00:48:50,594 --> 00:48:51,928
Running on a snowy path…

1135
00:48:53,096 --> 00:48:54,348
- It's romantic.
- Right.

1136
00:48:54,890 --> 00:48:57,893
It's so exciting to run on a snowy path.

1137
00:48:57,976 --> 00:48:59,186
- Are you excited?
- Yes.

1138
00:49:00,354 --> 00:49:02,272
You find this exciting?

1139
00:49:04,149 --> 00:49:05,734
- It's exciting!
- It's exciting.

1140
00:49:07,277 --> 00:49:09,154
<i>Yeon-koung asked, so I went running.</i>

1141
00:49:09,237 --> 00:49:11,198
<i>It did feel nice to get some fresh air.</i>

1142
00:49:11,823 --> 00:49:13,909
<i>I was always busy</i>
<i>playing volleyball in the winter,</i>

1143
00:49:13,992 --> 00:49:16,411
<i>so I never got to enjoy any winter sports.</i>

1144
00:49:16,495 --> 00:49:19,331
<i>I knew I wouldn't experience</i>
<i>something like this anywhere else.</i>

1145
00:49:19,414 --> 00:49:21,625
<i>It was like a dream</i>
<i>on my bucket list came true.</i>

1146
00:49:22,876 --> 00:49:25,712
<i>It was snowy everywhere,</i>
<i>and with all those hills,</i>

1147
00:49:25,796 --> 00:49:28,548
<i>it looked like</i>
<i>a beautiful scene from a fairy tale.</i>

1148
00:49:30,967 --> 00:49:31,843
It's uphill.

1149
00:49:32,511 --> 00:49:33,470
Oh, no.

1150
00:49:34,179 --> 00:49:35,138
- Hold on.
- Geez.

1151
00:49:35,222 --> 00:49:36,223
This is so…

1152
00:49:37,599 --> 00:49:38,558
Again?

1153
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:42,688
THE HILL GETS STEEPER

1154
00:49:42,771 --> 00:49:43,980
What's up with this hill?

1155
00:49:45,232 --> 00:49:46,650
How do we go up this?

1156
00:49:48,777 --> 00:49:49,903
This uphill is too tough.

1157
00:49:50,612 --> 00:49:52,280
I'll put the B&B on flat land next time.

1158
00:49:53,782 --> 00:49:54,616
I'm so tired.

1159
00:49:54,700 --> 00:49:56,993
MORNING RUN ENDS

1160
00:49:57,077 --> 00:49:58,870
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work.

1161
00:49:58,954 --> 00:49:59,871
Good job, everyone.

1162
00:49:59,955 --> 00:50:01,456
Good job.

1163
00:50:01,957 --> 00:50:03,375
Good work.

1164
00:50:03,458 --> 00:50:06,044
LET'S CLOSE THE DOOR

1165
00:50:06,586 --> 00:50:07,462
Damn it.

1166
00:50:10,799 --> 00:50:12,300
IT'S HARDER WHEN CLOSING IT

1167
00:50:12,384 --> 00:50:14,219
- You can just…
- I'll hold you.

1168
00:50:14,302 --> 00:50:15,512
You don't have to.

1169
00:50:15,595 --> 00:50:16,888
- You can just…
- Okay.

1170
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:19,141
HE LEARNED HOW TO CLOSE IT BY DAY 2

1171
00:50:19,224 --> 00:50:20,183
How do you close it?

1172
00:50:21,601 --> 00:50:22,602
You can reach it?

1173
00:50:22,686 --> 00:50:23,854
Like this.

1174
00:50:23,937 --> 00:50:24,896
Gosh, you…

1175
00:50:25,689 --> 00:50:26,606
Hey.

1176
00:50:27,274 --> 00:50:28,859
Pull it more or it'll open.

1177
00:50:31,027 --> 00:50:32,529
I think it's enough.

1178
00:50:32,612 --> 00:50:33,572
Okay.

1179
00:50:33,655 --> 00:50:34,823
I'm so tired.

1180
00:50:35,824 --> 00:50:37,200
Gosh, I'm so tired.

1181
00:50:40,036 --> 00:50:40,871
SNEEZING

1182
00:50:41,997 --> 00:50:43,498
I feel dizzy.

1183
00:50:44,332 --> 00:50:45,751
Boss, are you okay?

1184
00:50:45,834 --> 00:50:47,836
I don't think I can move.

1185
00:50:47,919 --> 00:50:49,254
I'm exhausted.

1186
00:50:49,838 --> 00:50:51,798
OUT OF ENERGY AFTER RUN

1187
00:50:58,096 --> 00:51:00,015
YEON-KOUNG WORKS OUT SOME MORE

1188
00:51:01,975 --> 00:51:04,102
- Hi, Jun-ho. Did you sleep well?
- What about you?

1189
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:05,604
We went out to run.

1190
00:51:05,687 --> 00:51:08,190
I know. And you're on the bike
after running?

1191
00:51:08,273 --> 00:51:10,192
- We only did one lap.
- Really?

1192
00:51:10,275 --> 00:51:11,818
- The uphill…
- It was too steep?

1193
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:12,736
Yeah.

1194
00:51:12,819 --> 00:51:15,280
And you're working out more inside.

1195
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:27,375
WORKING HARD

1196
00:51:33,423 --> 00:51:35,091
SHE FINISHES THE 30-MIN WORKOUT

1197
00:51:37,219 --> 00:51:40,263
GETTING READY FOR WORK

1198
00:51:41,848 --> 00:51:48,230
THE YOUNGEST WAKES UP

1199
00:51:54,152 --> 00:51:58,698
CRAWLING

1200
00:52:04,246 --> 00:52:07,707
GETTING READY FOR WORK

1201
00:52:07,791 --> 00:52:10,168
THE BOSS WAKES UP AGAIN

1202
00:52:10,252 --> 00:52:11,086
It's cold.

1203
00:52:13,713 --> 00:52:17,467
RUBBING THE SLEEP FROM HIS EYES

1204
00:52:17,551 --> 00:52:19,469
THE BOSS WASHES UP TOO

1205
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:23,932
DROPS ON THE FLOOR

1206
00:52:30,564 --> 00:52:32,732
WHILE OTHERS GOT READY FOR WORK

1207
00:52:35,026 --> 00:52:37,195
JUN-HO PREPARED SOME FRUIT

1208
00:52:37,279 --> 00:52:38,905
- Have some of these.
- We can eat these?

1209
00:52:38,989 --> 00:52:40,699
- You can.
- Do we get breakfast too?

1210
00:52:42,117 --> 00:52:44,286
- Do you like strawberries? And grapes?
- Yes.

1211
00:52:44,369 --> 00:52:45,537
Shine Muscats.

1212
00:52:50,667 --> 00:52:53,670
So you four will go
everywhere together today?

1213
00:52:53,753 --> 00:52:55,338
- Yes.
- And come back together?

1214
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:56,882
Our plans were the same.

1215
00:52:56,965 --> 00:52:58,300
- Right.
- That's perfect.

1216
00:52:58,967 --> 00:53:00,594
You'll become a lot closer.

1217
00:53:01,261 --> 00:53:02,762
- Be safe.
- Okay.

1218
00:53:02,846 --> 00:53:04,431
- What about the tops?
- Give them to me.

1219
00:53:04,514 --> 00:53:05,932
- Thank you.
- I'll take them.

1220
00:53:06,016 --> 00:53:06,975
Thank you.

1221
00:53:07,058 --> 00:53:08,685
STRAWBERRY TOPS IN HIS HANDS

1222
00:53:08,768 --> 00:53:10,186
- I'll take your waste.
- Thank you.

1223
00:53:10,270 --> 00:53:11,104
It's an honor.

1224
00:53:11,897 --> 00:53:13,064
- Have a safe trip.
- Okay.

1225
00:53:13,148 --> 00:53:14,316
SWEET JUN-HO

1226
00:53:14,399 --> 00:53:16,610
- What time will you be back?
- Around 5:00 p.m.

1227
00:53:16,693 --> 00:53:18,653
- At 5:00 p.m.? Have a safe trip.
- Okay.

1228
00:53:18,737 --> 00:53:19,988
- See you later.
- See you later.

1229
00:53:20,071 --> 00:53:21,323
- See you later.
- Have fun.

1230
00:53:21,406 --> 00:53:22,532
GUEST JUN-HO

1231
00:53:22,616 --> 00:53:24,117
SMITA, SNEHAL

1232
00:53:24,200 --> 00:53:26,036
EVERYONE'S GONE ON THEIR TRIPS

1233
00:53:29,539 --> 00:53:31,333
- Everyone left?
- Yeah.

1234
00:53:31,416 --> 00:53:32,709
KIAN'S B&B IS EMPTY NOW

1235
00:53:32,792 --> 00:53:34,294
Did you sleep well? Do you feel sick?

1236
00:53:34,377 --> 00:53:35,211
I was cold.

1237
00:53:36,296 --> 00:53:37,714
We should clean up in a bit.

1238
00:53:37,797 --> 00:53:38,840
10:30 A.M.

1239
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:41,968
Okay, we have until 5:00 p.m.,
and what we have to do is clean.

1240
00:53:42,052 --> 00:53:42,969
Clean.

1241
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:45,180
And we should prepare
for unexpected guests.

1242
00:53:45,805 --> 00:53:46,973
Tell me what we need.

1243
00:53:47,057 --> 00:53:49,434
- I'll go by myself and…
- Alone?

1244
00:53:49,517 --> 00:53:51,186
I'll buy everything really fast.

1245
00:53:51,269 --> 00:53:54,189
- Then, I'll clean up.
- Okay. I won't take long.

1246
00:53:54,272 --> 00:53:55,982
- I'll be back.
- Bye.

1247
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:56,900
- Jun-ho.
- Yes?

1248
00:53:56,983 --> 00:53:58,234
Have lunch while you're out.

1249
00:53:58,318 --> 00:53:59,152
Lunch?

1250
00:53:59,235 --> 00:54:01,738
It's 10:30 a.m.,
so won't you be back at lunchtime?

1251
00:54:01,821 --> 00:54:02,739
Let's eat together.

1252
00:54:02,822 --> 00:54:04,741
Okay. I'm actually hungry.

1253
00:54:04,824 --> 00:54:05,909
You are?

1254
00:54:06,743 --> 00:54:07,869
I should eat some snacks.

1255
00:54:08,453 --> 00:54:10,080
You can eat. I'm all right.

1256
00:54:10,163 --> 00:54:11,081
Okay.

1257
00:54:19,631 --> 00:54:21,216
KIAN'S B&B

1258
00:54:21,299 --> 00:54:22,634
- Let's clean.
- Yes, Boss.

1259
00:54:23,259 --> 00:54:25,220
CLEANING BEGINS

1260
00:54:25,303 --> 00:54:26,596
Gosh, it's dusty.

1261
00:54:32,686 --> 00:54:34,062
Geez, the house is…

1262
00:54:39,025 --> 00:54:40,443
The house's too big.

1263
00:54:44,531 --> 00:54:45,991
It is pretty dirty.

1264
00:54:46,074 --> 00:54:48,368
- There's a lot of dust.
- There is.

1265
00:54:48,994 --> 00:54:50,453
After doing this,

1266
00:54:50,537 --> 00:54:52,372
if we use a lint roller, it'll be clean.

1267
00:54:52,455 --> 00:54:53,289
Okay.

1268
00:54:53,373 --> 00:54:55,250
THE YOUNGEST SWEEPS THE FLOOR

1269
00:54:59,129 --> 00:55:02,090
YEON-KOUNG REMOVES DUST
WITH A LINT ROLLER

1270
00:55:02,173 --> 00:55:07,137
AND THE BOSS CLEANS EVERY CORNER

1271
00:55:19,274 --> 00:55:20,942
- I think…
- Yeah?

1272
00:55:21,026 --> 00:55:23,987
- The entrance should always be clean.
- Right.

1273
00:55:24,070 --> 00:55:26,031
So we should clean it.

1274
00:55:26,823 --> 00:55:28,950
DIRTY

1275
00:55:29,034 --> 00:55:30,160
Want to dust the mat?

1276
00:55:30,243 --> 00:55:31,995
- How?
- We'll bring it outside.

1277
00:55:32,620 --> 00:55:34,039
BY THE WAY THE ENTRANCE MAT IS

1278
00:55:34,622 --> 00:55:35,582
HUGE LIKE KIAN'S B&B

1279
00:55:35,665 --> 00:55:37,792
1 YEON-KOUNG
1.5 YEON-KOUNG

1280
00:55:43,673 --> 00:55:45,341
Okay.

1281
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:49,929
Okay, take it out.

1282
00:55:50,013 --> 00:55:50,847
Bring it out.

1283
00:55:53,016 --> 00:55:53,975
Geez.

1284
00:55:54,059 --> 00:55:55,310
Zuha, go and bring it out.

1285
00:55:55,393 --> 00:55:56,478
- The mop.
- The mop.

1286
00:55:56,561 --> 00:55:58,480
A MOP TO DUST A MAT OFF?

1287
00:55:58,563 --> 00:56:00,023
- You hit it.
- Hit it with that.

1288
00:56:00,106 --> 00:56:01,608
- Okay.
- The opposite side.

1289
00:56:01,691 --> 00:56:03,443
- Like this?
- Yeah, hit it with that.

1290
00:56:03,526 --> 00:56:04,527
Like this?

1291
00:56:05,111 --> 00:56:06,112
Hit it.

1292
00:56:06,196 --> 00:56:07,280
- There you go.
- No!

1293
00:56:07,363 --> 00:56:09,115
- Hit it like this.
- How? Like this?

1294
00:56:09,199 --> 00:56:11,034
LIKE THIS?

1295
00:56:14,871 --> 00:56:15,705
No.

1296
00:56:16,289 --> 00:56:17,791
No? What's wrong?

1297
00:56:17,874 --> 00:56:19,250
Hit with the side of the handle.

1298
00:56:19,334 --> 00:56:21,503
Hit the mat with the side, not the tip.

1299
00:56:21,586 --> 00:56:22,420
SIDE? TIP?

1300
00:56:22,504 --> 00:56:23,588
How do you do that?

1301
00:56:23,671 --> 00:56:25,673
- Make the dust shake off.
- Make it shake off.

1302
00:56:27,300 --> 00:56:28,343
Harder.

1303
00:56:31,763 --> 00:56:33,431
You hold this.

1304
00:56:34,224 --> 00:56:36,184
SUBSTITUTION

1305
00:56:37,018 --> 00:56:37,977
What's the difference?

1306
00:56:38,061 --> 00:56:39,104
One, two, three.

1307
00:56:39,187 --> 00:56:40,396
- I'll hit hard.
- Okay.

1308
00:56:40,480 --> 00:56:42,649
- Slant it a bit.
- Slant it?

1309
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:51,574
NOT THAT DIFFERENT

1310
00:56:52,283 --> 00:56:53,368
What on earth?

1311
00:56:53,451 --> 00:56:54,869
STILL DUSTY

1312
00:56:54,953 --> 00:56:56,746
- Geez.
- It's not working.

1313
00:56:57,580 --> 00:56:58,665
Flip it.

1314
00:56:58,748 --> 00:56:59,666
Flip it?

1315
00:57:01,417 --> 00:57:03,378
Lift it and flip it.

1316
00:57:03,461 --> 00:57:04,629
We did flip it.

1317
00:57:04,712 --> 00:57:06,131
No, like this.

1318
00:57:06,214 --> 00:57:07,549
Switch.

1319
00:57:07,632 --> 00:57:09,300
- Switch.
- Slant it.

1320
00:57:10,051 --> 00:57:12,095
Okay, pull on it more.

1321
00:57:16,933 --> 00:57:18,017
The dust is coming off.

1322
00:57:18,101 --> 00:57:19,686
- Right.
- It's working.

1323
00:57:19,769 --> 00:57:20,979
Hit harder.

1324
00:57:21,813 --> 00:57:22,897
HIT THE BOSS HARD

1325
00:57:24,524 --> 00:57:25,358
Geez.

1326
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:26,401
I think it's enough.

1327
00:57:26,484 --> 00:57:27,569
- It's enough.
- Let's go.

1328
00:57:27,652 --> 00:57:28,486
Good work.

1329
00:57:28,570 --> 00:57:29,779
THEY FINISH DUSTING THE MAT

1330
00:57:29,863 --> 00:57:30,864
Okay.

1331
00:57:31,364 --> 00:57:32,282
It's clean.

1332
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:36,411
All right.

1333
00:57:36,494 --> 00:57:37,495
THE DOOR

1334
00:57:37,579 --> 00:57:38,580
NEEDS TO BE

1335
00:57:38,663 --> 00:57:40,582
CLOSED AGAIN

1336
00:57:40,665 --> 00:57:42,250
Let's keep it open.

1337
00:57:42,333 --> 00:57:43,918
Let's keep it open for a bit.

1338
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:45,128
VENTILATING

1339
00:57:45,211 --> 00:57:48,298
Hey, we should wipe down
all the slippers with wet wipes.

1340
00:57:48,381 --> 00:57:49,299
The bottoms.

1341
00:57:49,382 --> 00:57:50,550
The bottoms of the slippers?

1342
00:57:50,633 --> 00:57:51,509
Yes.

1343
00:57:51,593 --> 00:57:53,428
Let's use a rag. Wet wipes are a waste.

1344
00:57:53,511 --> 00:57:54,512
A rag? Okay.

1345
00:57:56,931 --> 00:58:02,145
WASHING A RAG TO USE INSTEAD OF WET WIPES

1346
00:58:06,649 --> 00:58:10,653
HE CLEANS THE SINK WHILE HE'S AT IT

1347
00:58:13,364 --> 00:58:15,825
WASHES HIS FACE

1348
00:58:16,743 --> 00:58:18,620
AND TIDIES HIS SIDEBURNS

1349
00:58:25,793 --> 00:58:26,669
Use a rag.

1350
00:58:28,671 --> 00:58:31,257
We'll clean these
since we cleaned the house.

1351
00:58:33,968 --> 00:58:35,678
WITH ONE RAG

1352
00:58:36,262 --> 00:58:38,765
WIPING VIGOROUSLY

1353
00:58:47,440 --> 00:58:48,650
What?

1354
00:58:48,733 --> 00:58:51,110
- What on earth is this?
- What?

1355
00:58:51,194 --> 00:58:52,904
What's with this show?

1356
00:58:52,987 --> 00:58:53,905
This show?

1357
00:58:53,988 --> 00:58:55,532
It's like a cleaning show.

1358
00:58:55,615 --> 00:58:59,327
I just had reality hit me hard
while cleaning these slippers like this.

1359
00:59:01,412 --> 00:59:03,581
Hey, you can't come back
even if you want to.

1360
00:59:03,665 --> 00:59:05,041
Every day is so precious.

1361
00:59:05,124 --> 00:59:07,126
I mean, what on earth are we doing?

1362
00:59:07,210 --> 00:59:08,086
Hopes and dreams.

1363
00:59:09,379 --> 00:59:10,213
Geez.

1364
00:59:10,296 --> 00:59:12,674
KIAN'S B&B OF HOPE AND DREAMS

1365
00:59:12,757 --> 00:59:14,884
When we have new guests come in,

1366
00:59:14,968 --> 00:59:17,428
we should put their suitcases there
and use these rags.

1367
00:59:17,512 --> 00:59:20,223
- Wipe them? Okay.
- Let's wipe the wheels before they enter.

1368
00:59:20,306 --> 00:59:21,599
We should wipe them down.

1369
00:59:21,683 --> 00:59:22,809
Then, it'll be cleaner here.

1370
00:59:22,892 --> 00:59:25,061
KIAN'S B&B RULES
CLEAN GUESTS' SUITCASES WHEN THEY COME

1371
00:59:25,144 --> 00:59:25,979
Let's wrap up.

1372
00:59:26,062 --> 00:59:27,397
Let's tidy this up first.

1373
00:59:28,898 --> 00:59:30,149
Geez.

1374
00:59:30,233 --> 00:59:31,150
What on earth?

1375
00:59:32,151 --> 00:59:33,486
Boss, what's this?

1376
00:59:33,987 --> 00:59:35,196
What is it?

1377
00:59:35,280 --> 00:59:36,239
What?

1378
00:59:36,322 --> 00:59:37,782
THE SLIPPERS GOT DIRTY

1379
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:39,409
What?

1380
00:59:41,244 --> 00:59:42,203
He's driving me crazy.

1381
00:59:42,287 --> 00:59:43,871
THE CULPRIT

1382
00:59:43,955 --> 00:59:46,708
Are you serious? We just cleaned them.

1383
00:59:47,875 --> 00:59:49,210
Sorry about that.

1384
00:59:50,336 --> 00:59:51,254
I'm sorry.

1385
00:59:51,838 --> 00:59:52,797
10 MINUTES EARLIER

1386
00:59:52,880 --> 00:59:53,715
Let's take them all.

1387
00:59:54,799 --> 00:59:57,218
HE WENT TO THE STORAGE

1388
00:59:57,302 --> 00:59:59,429
IN THE SLIPPERS

1389
00:59:59,512 --> 01:00:01,889
I'm sorry. I should've set an example.

1390
01:00:02,807 --> 01:00:03,641
I'm sorry.

1391
01:00:03,725 --> 01:00:05,476
Clean those slippers later.

1392
01:00:05,560 --> 01:00:06,394
Okay.

1393
01:00:07,270 --> 01:00:08,521
Aren't you hungry?

1394
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:09,731
- What?
- I'm hungry.

1395
01:00:09,814 --> 01:00:10,648
It's lunchtime.

1396
01:00:10,732 --> 01:00:11,566
12:30 P.M.

1397
01:00:11,649 --> 01:00:12,525
It is.

1398
01:00:12,609 --> 01:00:13,443
Let's eat first.

1399
01:00:13,526 --> 01:00:14,694
Yeah, we should.

1400
01:00:14,777 --> 01:00:16,362
I'm hungry.

1401
01:00:21,242 --> 01:00:22,327
What do we eat?

1402
01:00:22,410 --> 01:00:23,620
<i>Ramyeon</i> and leftover rice?

1403
01:00:23,703 --> 01:00:25,288
- I think that's better.
- Right.

1404
01:00:25,371 --> 01:00:28,416
I'll ask Jun-ho where he is,
so we can eat together.

1405
01:00:29,292 --> 01:00:30,251
Where are you?

1406
01:00:30,335 --> 01:00:31,377
I'm almost there.

1407
01:00:31,461 --> 01:00:33,713
Hurry up. We're making the <i>ramyeon </i>now.

1408
01:00:33,796 --> 01:00:36,007
<i>Okay, I'll be there soon.</i>
<i>Go ahead and eat first.</i>

1409
01:00:36,090 --> 01:00:37,091
Okay.

1410
01:00:41,763 --> 01:00:42,930
I'll add a bit of kimchi.

1411
01:00:43,848 --> 01:00:45,642
ADDING KIMCHI TO <i>RAMYEON </i>BROTH

1412
01:00:47,435 --> 01:00:48,519
ONE MORE TIME

1413
01:00:50,938 --> 01:00:51,898
Ham?

1414
01:00:51,981 --> 01:00:52,940
Ham?

1415
01:00:55,443 --> 01:00:56,903
ADDING HAM BROKEN UP BY SCISSORS

1416
01:01:02,909 --> 01:01:04,494
This is going to be so good.

1417
01:01:05,495 --> 01:01:06,329
It does look good.

1418
01:01:06,412 --> 01:01:07,538
Shall we dig in?

1419
01:01:09,332 --> 01:01:11,167
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you.

1420
01:01:11,250 --> 01:01:12,293
Enjoy.

1421
01:01:28,893 --> 01:01:30,770
It's good. You cooked it really well.

1422
01:01:37,652 --> 01:01:39,362
You don't gain much weight, right?

1423
01:01:39,445 --> 01:01:40,613
I do if I eat a lot.

1424
01:01:40,697 --> 01:01:41,948
I need to watch my diet.

1425
01:01:42,532 --> 01:01:43,366
Really?

1426
01:01:43,449 --> 01:01:47,078
When I was an athlete,
I didn't eat unhealthy stuff,

1427
01:01:47,161 --> 01:01:49,580
like fried food or flour-based food.

1428
01:01:49,664 --> 01:01:51,457
And as soon as I retired,

1429
01:01:51,541 --> 01:01:53,710
I ate a ton of it for over a month.

1430
01:01:54,335 --> 01:01:55,920
I ate everything I wanted to eat.

1431
01:01:56,003 --> 01:01:57,547
I even drank every day.

1432
01:01:57,630 --> 01:01:59,465
Then, when I got a checkup,

1433
01:01:59,549 --> 01:02:00,925
they said I had high cholesterol.

1434
01:02:01,759 --> 01:02:02,760
- You?
- Really?

1435
01:02:02,844 --> 01:02:04,095
And a high liver somatic index.

1436
01:02:04,178 --> 01:02:05,763
- Really?
- Right away.

1437
01:02:05,847 --> 01:02:08,975
It happened in just two months.
So, I decided to get it together.

1438
01:02:09,058 --> 01:02:10,560
- So I do it every day.
- Work out?

1439
01:02:10,643 --> 01:02:12,061
Even just a little bit.

1440
01:02:12,145 --> 01:02:13,104
- Work out?
- Yeah.

1441
01:02:13,187 --> 01:02:14,272
Exercising?

1442
01:02:14,355 --> 01:02:16,774
By the way, I saw the scenery
after running.

1443
01:02:16,858 --> 01:02:18,443
- It was amazing.
- Beautiful?

1444
01:02:18,526 --> 01:02:19,360
It really was.

1445
01:02:19,444 --> 01:02:20,653
- Is that so?
- Yeah.

1446
01:02:20,737 --> 01:02:22,530
We should go check that out.

1447
01:02:23,114 --> 01:02:24,657
The river. Right.

1448
01:02:24,741 --> 01:02:26,868
It's frozen, so I think it'll be fun.

1449
01:02:26,951 --> 01:02:27,785
With the sled.

1450
01:02:27,869 --> 01:02:29,620
- Right.
- The ice sled.

1451
01:02:29,704 --> 01:02:30,997
I've never done it before.

1452
01:02:31,080 --> 01:02:32,623
- Never? Ice sleds?
- No.

1453
01:02:34,876 --> 01:02:36,586
THE LAKE SURROUNDING KIAN'S B&B

1454
01:02:37,462 --> 01:02:41,591
TODAY'S EVENT FOR KIAN'S B&B
RIDING THE ICE SLEDS

1455
01:02:42,175 --> 01:02:43,134
Gosh.

1456
01:02:43,217 --> 01:02:45,803
JUN-HO IS BACK FROM GROCERY SHOPPING

1457
01:02:46,929 --> 01:02:47,889
HIS HANDS ARE FULL

1458
01:02:47,972 --> 01:02:49,307
Right, the coffee.

1459
01:02:49,390 --> 01:02:50,349
Okay.

1460
01:02:54,145 --> 01:02:55,188
Welcome back. Come on up.

1461
01:02:55,271 --> 01:02:56,272
Come eat <i>ramyeon.</i>

1462
01:02:58,775 --> 01:03:00,526
- Welcome back.
- He's here.

1463
01:03:01,027 --> 01:03:01,861
Here.

1464
01:03:02,862 --> 01:03:03,988
Thanks.

1465
01:03:04,572 --> 01:03:05,656
Good job.

1466
01:03:06,282 --> 01:03:07,533
Should I add rice?

1467
01:03:07,617 --> 01:03:09,118
- Add it?
- Yeah. I think that's better.

1468
01:03:09,202 --> 01:03:10,620
- Let's do it.
- It'll be better.

1469
01:03:17,001 --> 01:03:18,211
- It is good.
- Yeah.

1470
01:03:21,631 --> 01:03:23,716
<i>Ramyeon</i> tastes the best
in places like this.

1471
01:03:23,800 --> 01:03:25,051
- Right?
- Yeah.

1472
01:03:25,843 --> 01:03:26,677
It's good.

1473
01:03:26,761 --> 01:03:30,598
Later, when they come back
at around 5:00 p.m.,

1474
01:03:30,681 --> 01:03:32,725
we're going to go ride
the ice sled at the river.

1475
01:03:33,309 --> 01:03:35,061
- That sounds good.
- Together.

1476
01:03:35,144 --> 01:03:36,062
This is delicious.

1477
01:03:37,146 --> 01:03:39,524
1:00 P.M.

1478
01:03:41,317 --> 01:03:42,902
Hey, let's take a break.

1479
01:03:43,528 --> 01:03:44,403
I'm sleepy.

1480
01:03:45,029 --> 01:03:46,447
You're sleeping right away?

1481
01:03:46,531 --> 01:03:47,740
I'll just lie down for a bit.

1482
01:03:48,783 --> 01:03:50,284
Why do I like lying down so much?

1483
01:03:50,368 --> 01:03:51,869
Maybe my time's coming?

1484
01:03:51,953 --> 01:03:53,204
I'm lying down so often.

1485
01:03:53,287 --> 01:03:55,540
Hey, your runny nose
has improved from yesterday.

1486
01:03:55,623 --> 01:03:56,999
- It stopped running.
- That's good.

1487
01:03:57,083 --> 01:03:58,334
Yeah. You got better.

1488
01:03:59,293 --> 01:04:01,170
TIME TO SLEEP

1489
01:04:01,254 --> 01:04:03,297
God, it's so cold.

1490
01:04:04,298 --> 01:04:06,342
THEY DIDN'T CLOSE THE DOOR EARLIER

1491
01:04:06,425 --> 01:04:10,096
THE SHOES THEY TOOK OUTSIDE EARLIER

1492
01:04:14,058 --> 01:04:20,773
HE BRINGS THE SHOES IN
BEFORE HE GOES TO SLEEP

1493
01:04:24,235 --> 01:04:26,654
Boss wants to rest, but he can't.

1494
01:04:27,738 --> 01:04:29,490
Kian, do we have any tape?

1495
01:04:30,825 --> 01:04:31,868
- Tape?
- Yes.

1496
01:04:32,702 --> 01:04:34,036
I have to go to the storage.

1497
01:04:34,704 --> 01:04:39,166
HE VISITS THE STORAGE
BEFORE HE GOES TO SLEEP

1498
01:04:39,250 --> 01:04:40,084
It's not here.

1499
01:04:43,254 --> 01:04:46,966
HE CLOSES THE DOOR BEFORE HE GOES TO SLEEP

1500
01:04:49,176 --> 01:04:53,014
HE CLIMBS THE SOFA BEFORE HE GOES TO SLEEP

1501
01:05:00,313 --> 01:05:01,147
I'm so tired.

1502
01:05:07,612 --> 01:05:08,738
Are you okay?

1503
01:05:08,821 --> 01:05:09,655
Gosh.

1504
01:05:09,739 --> 01:05:12,450
WHILE THE BOSS IS TAKING A REST

1505
01:05:12,533 --> 01:05:14,577
We have to clean the bathroom.

1506
01:05:14,660 --> 01:05:16,412
THE EMPLOYEES FINISH UP THE CLEANING

1507
01:05:16,495 --> 01:05:20,124
CLEANING THE BATHROOM

1508
01:05:21,250 --> 01:05:23,628
CLEANING THE SAUNA

1509
01:05:24,378 --> 01:05:26,255
AND JUN-HO DOES THE DISHES

1510
01:05:29,508 --> 01:05:32,887
They said they'd be back around 5:00 p.m.

1511
01:05:32,970 --> 01:05:33,846
What about us?

1512
01:05:33,930 --> 01:05:36,015
It's already 2:00 p.m.
We have three hours left.

1513
01:05:36,098 --> 01:05:39,977
Before I went to sleep last night,
I watched your "SPAGHETTI" video.

1514
01:05:40,061 --> 01:05:41,145
You did? Gosh.

1515
01:05:41,228 --> 01:05:42,521
You looked totally different.

1516
01:05:42,605 --> 01:05:43,814
- Really?
- Seriously.

1517
01:05:43,898 --> 01:05:44,941
You're a flirt on stage.

1518
01:05:50,196 --> 01:05:51,447
Like this. What is that?

1519
01:05:51,530 --> 01:05:52,823
A DIFFERENT SIDE OF THE YOUNGEST

1520
01:05:52,907 --> 01:05:54,450
It wasn't the Kazuha I knew.

1521
01:05:54,533 --> 01:05:55,368
Like this.

1522
01:05:56,327 --> 01:05:57,745
I was shocked.

1523
01:05:57,828 --> 01:05:59,163
You're good at that.

1524
01:05:59,246 --> 01:06:00,081
- Right?
- She is.

1525
01:06:00,164 --> 01:06:01,165
You're good.

1526
01:06:01,248 --> 01:06:04,126
How you are in everyday life
is also a totally different

1527
01:06:04,210 --> 01:06:06,379
from when you're playing on the court.

1528
01:06:06,462 --> 01:06:08,631
Of course.
I can fool around like this here.

1529
01:06:08,714 --> 01:06:11,342
But over there,
I was a professional.

1530
01:06:11,425 --> 01:06:12,802
- Right.
- It's different.

1531
01:06:12,885 --> 01:06:16,013
All of your younger colleagues
must be scared of you now.

1532
01:06:16,097 --> 01:06:17,682
Do they act awkward or scared?

1533
01:06:18,683 --> 01:06:19,600
I think both.

1534
01:06:19,684 --> 01:06:21,310
I thought I'd be too.

1535
01:06:21,394 --> 01:06:23,270
- What?
- But I was surprised you were so kind.

1536
01:06:23,354 --> 01:06:25,606
Really? Do I look kind of cold?

1537
01:06:26,190 --> 01:06:28,192
Rather than cold…

1538
01:06:28,275 --> 01:06:30,152
- Fierce? Right.
- You have that fierce presence.

1539
01:06:30,236 --> 01:06:32,363
Really? It must be
because I'm always yelling.

1540
01:06:32,446 --> 01:06:34,991
Normally, I'm not like that though.

1541
01:06:36,242 --> 01:06:37,785
We have free time right now.

1542
01:06:37,868 --> 01:06:39,286
- Should we go somewhere?
- Should we?

1543
01:06:39,370 --> 01:06:40,329
- Yes.
- Yeah?

1544
01:06:40,413 --> 01:06:41,622
Where are you going?

1545
01:06:41,706 --> 01:06:43,457
Gosh, weren't you sleeping?

1546
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:44,750
Where are you going?

1547
01:06:44,834 --> 01:06:45,668
Well…

1548
01:06:45,751 --> 01:06:49,046
It'd be nice to go check out Sky Ranch
or one of those places.

1549
01:06:49,130 --> 01:06:50,423
SKY RANCH

1550
01:06:50,506 --> 01:06:51,757
It's only 22 minutes from here.

1551
01:06:52,425 --> 01:06:53,551
It's nearby.

1552
01:06:53,634 --> 01:06:54,885
- What do you say?
- Sounds good.

1553
01:06:57,555 --> 01:06:58,556
- Want to go?
- Yeah.

1554
01:06:58,639 --> 01:07:00,641
Let's go then. It won't take long.

1555
01:07:01,267 --> 01:07:02,810
Why do I feel so weak?

1556
01:07:02,893 --> 01:07:04,395
You'll feel better once you go.

1557
01:07:05,146 --> 01:07:06,313
Let's go.

1558
01:07:14,739 --> 01:07:16,282
Let's go, Kian.

1559
01:07:16,365 --> 01:07:18,159
- You're driving, Jun-ho?
- Yes.

1560
01:07:19,118 --> 01:07:21,787
SKY RANCH

1561
01:07:21,871 --> 01:07:23,914
It's nice to go somewhere like this.

1562
01:07:23,998 --> 01:07:27,043
Yeah, I didn't think
we'd have time for something like this.

1563
01:07:27,835 --> 01:07:28,878
This is nice.

1564
01:07:29,545 --> 01:07:32,214
Did Jae-eun's pair
and Don-hee's pair go separately?

1565
01:07:32,298 --> 01:07:34,383
- No, the four of them went together.
- Together.

1566
01:07:35,259 --> 01:07:37,011
I hope something happens between them.

1567
01:07:37,595 --> 01:07:39,221
- Yeah.
- You can't help but smile at them.

1568
01:07:39,305 --> 01:07:40,473
Yeah.

1569
01:07:42,016 --> 01:07:44,393
ANMOKHAEBYEON BEACH

1570
01:07:44,477 --> 01:07:45,770
- It's the ocean!
- It's the ocean!

1571
01:07:45,853 --> 01:07:46,771
